<!-- Conclusion -->
<section id="sec-conclusion" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>Master All Six Ratios With One Triangle</h2>
  <p>Every ratio on this page comes from the same three sides and one reference angle. Label the triangle, match the side pair to the mode, and let the calculator do the arithmetic. Sine, cosine, and tangent answer the direct comparisons; cosecant, secant, and cotangent flip them. SOH-CAH-TOA recalls the first three, the reciprocal rule recalls the rest, and the identity sin squared plus cos squared equals 1 ties sine and cosine together. Verify with the Pythagorean check and the reciprocal products, then return to the calculator at the top of this page to run your numbers.</p>
</section>
